[Music]  [Applause]  welcome back everyone mark man and rip  here with playstation competition center  today's topic is the various ways you  can use soul gauge in soul calibur 6.  yeah let's learn the different offensive  and defensive uses for this particular  meter  this curved bar next to your health is  called the soul gauge you build this  gauge largely by attacking although  blocking attacks will still earn you a  small amount  each time you complete the gauge you  earn one stock you can hold up to two  stocks at once  it's worth noting that the reversal  engine mechanic which we cover more  deeply in a separate video  earns a huge amount of meter also when  your opponent is one round away from  winning you will get an entire stock of  meter for free  there are three primary ways sole gauge  is spent until caliber six and each use  costs a full stock  meter the first is a defensive option  called soul charge  to activate soul charge you simply hold  back and press r2 or all three attacks  your character will emit a burst of  energy and your soul gauge will begin  ticking down  when this timer reaches the bottom  you'll exit the soul charge mode  when you're install charge all of your  attacks do a small amount of damage even  when they're guarded  but beyond that soul park powers up each  character in completely different ways  for most certain attacks become enhanced  they may gain new properties like break  attacks  do more damage or combo in different  ways several characters will even gain  access to entirely new moves and stances  which can drastically change how they  play to learn more about your favorite  character and how they benefit from soul  cards  access the combat lessons option from  the training mode  and then choose soul charging if you do  a quarter circle forward motion and  press r2 you'll perform with soul attack  which leaves you in soul charge mode  after why pick one method over the other  well the energy burst method is very  defensive you'll push the opponent away  and be  completely safe and counter attack  whether they guarded the burst or not  use this if you're being pressured and  need a safe way to gain some space  the attack on the other hand is very  offensive soul attacks are risky used by  themselves and are easily dodged  but you can combo into them and they'll  keep your opponent close so you can  continue your offense with your sole  charge abilities  the other primary way to spend sole  gauges called critical aim simply press  r2 to activate a highly damaging super  attack  for your character  you can use critical edge attacks and  some combos to add extra damage or  if your opponent misses an attack right  next to you you can use the critical  edge to punish them for their mistake  as a final note there's a way to spend  50 of your soul gauge on a pairing  mechanic called resist impact  we covered that in our video on garden  packs we want to learn more about it  while critical edge may be flashy and  cool as a beginner you might want to opt  going for the defensive option  soul charge instead as it can get you  out of some tricky situations  that's all for this episode this  tutorial is made in partnership with the  playstation competition center team  you can sign up for open series  competitions on compete.playstation.com  subscribe to the bne esports channel for  more tutorials and soul calibur 6  content

